  "executive_briefing": "The global corporate tax and trade environment in 2026 is undergoing significant transformation driven by the operational enforcement of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax and escalating international tariff measures. Over 60 jurisdictions have enacted GloBE legislation, anchoring minimum effective tax rate monitoring for MNEs with revenues exceeding 750 million euros. Concurrently, new import tariffs announced globally are creating trade uncertainty, pushing multinational enterprises to heavily invest in real-time tax digitization, mandatory e-invoicing, and structured transactional data reporting to maintain compliance across complex cross-border frameworks.",
